     "text": "{\"count\": 3, \"rationale\": \"crown:obtain is an OR of three branches, so all three must be cut. (1) h4_1:reach depends only on h2_2:access, so it needs at least one block on its own. (2) h4_2:access is reachable through two independent routes: h2_1:obtain (from h1_2:traverse) and h3_1:access (from h2_3:pivot). (3) h4_0:obtain is an AND of h3_2, h3_1 and h2_0. No single block stops both h4_2 and h4_0. Blocking h4_2 leaves h4_0 fully reachable. Blocking h2_3 kills h4_0 but h4_2 survives via h2_1. Blocking h1_2 kills h2_0 and h2_1 but h4_2 survives via h3_1. So at least 3 blocks are needed, and 3 are enough, for example {h4_1, h4_2, h4_0} or {h2_2, h2_3, h1_2}.\"}"
    }
